{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>The appointed times of HaShem.</b> Rabbi Akiva said (Torat Kohanim, verse 35): these are the festival days on which labor is forbidden — end of quote. And it appears that for this reason Scripture concluded with <b>ומלבד מתנותיכם</b> etc., <b>כל נדריכם</b> etc., <b>כל נדבותיכם</b> which you give to HaShem — which implies even burnt offerings, and burnt offerings are not brought on a festival, as they said (Beitzah 19a): 'for you and not for Heaven' — so it is certain that the verse speaks only of the intermediate days of the festival (chol ha-mo'ed)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The abbreviation 'וגו׳' (etc.) is retained as in the original; the three bolded lemmata are the words following 'ומלבד' in Leviticus 23:38."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:00:37.723261401Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}